    {
      "text": "Persian has six bold whiskers that give it a look of toughness. The whiskers sense air movements to determine what is in the Pokémon’s surrounding vicinity. It becomes docile if grabbed by the whiskers.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Persian has six bold whiskers that give it a look of toughness. The whiskers sense air movements to determine what is in the Pokémon’s surrounding vicinity. It becomes docile if grabbed by the whiskers.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It has a violent temperament. It will attack anything that looks it in the eye. Its sharp claws inflict deep wounds.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It has a high opinion of itself, although not to the same extent as the Alolan Persian. It’s quite difficult to make friends with this Pokémon.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Although the jewel on its forehead appears to be a different color than those of Alolan Persian, it’s mostly made of the same material.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon is popular with rich people. It’s also targeted by hunters who are after the jewel in its forehead.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "The gem in its forehead glows on its own! It walks with all the grace and elegance of a proud queen.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "The gem in its forehead glows on its own! It walks with all the grace and elegance of a proud queen.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "Getting this prideful Pokémon to warm up to you takes a lot of effort, and it will claw at you the moment it gets annoyed.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its elegant and refined behavior clashes with that of the barbaric Perrserker. The relationship between the two is one of mutual disdain.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
